BT /F1 10 Tf 72 740 Td (HOLIDAYS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 727 Td ( ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 714 Td (10. Holiday year and entitlement. 10.1 The holiday year runs from 1 January to 31 December.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 701 Td (10.2 You are entitled to 25 days of paid holiday in each holiday year, in addition to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 688 Td (eight usual bank holidays in England. If you work part-time, your entitlement is reduced in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 675 Td (proportion. 10.3 After three complete years of employment, your holiday entitlement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 662 Td (increases to 27 days, and after five complete years to 28 days. 10.4 In the holiday year in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 649 Td (which your employment starts or ends, your entitlement is worked out in proportion to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 636 Td (part of the year you are employed, rounded up to the nearest half day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 623 Td ( ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 610 Td (11. Booking holiday. 11.1 You must book holiday through the HR system and have it approved) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 597 Td (by your manager before making any travel arrangements. 11.2 You must give at least twice as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 584 Td (much notice as the length of the holiday you want to take, and at least two weeks' notice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 571 Td (for any holiday of more than five days. 11.3 You may not take more than ten working days in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 558 Td (a row without the approval of your director. 11.4 The Company closes between Christmas and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 545 Td (New Year and you must keep three days of your entitlement for that period.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 532 Td ( ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 519 Td (12. Carrying holiday over. 12.1 You should take all of your holiday in the holiday year in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 506 Td (which it is earned. 12.2 You may carry over up to five days of unused holiday into the next) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 493 Td (holiday year, but you must take them by 31 March of that year or they will be lost. 12.3 If) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 480 Td (you could not take holiday because of sickness or family leave, you may carry over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 467 Td (holiday you were unable to take, and must use it within eighteen months of the end of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 454 Td (year in which it was earned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 441 Td ( ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 428 Td (12.4 Holiday on leaving. When your employment ends you will be paid for any holiday you have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 415 Td (earned in that year but not taken. If you have taken more holiday than you earned, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 402 Td (Company will deduct the excess from your final pay. Apart from this, the Company does not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 389 Td (pay in place of untaken holiday. 12.5 The Company may ask you to take any remaining holiday) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 376 Td (during your notice period.) Tj ET
endstream
